; M4 gate: CSM with the operators as tracks (driver.md §9, language.md §15).
; A note-less (fm3-csm voice) holds the patch, each fm3-N drives one operator's
; F-number and level — a formant — and the fm3-csm-rate track is the voice:
; its rates the pitch, its rest the breath, its end the voice's end. In CSM an
; operator's key is its level — TL on at its note, 127 at its gate or rest,
; $28 never keys CH3 — and a :vol table shapes the formant frame by frame.
(def-fm voice :alg 7 :fb 0
  :ar1 31 :rr1 15 :ks1 3 :tl1 20 :ml1 1
  :ar2 31 :rr2 15 :ks2 3 :tl2 24 :ml2 1
  :ar3 31 :rr3 15 :ks3 3 :tl3 30 :ml3 1
  :ar4 31 :rr4 15 :ks4 3 :tl4 36 :ml4 1)
(fm3-csm :tempo 120 voice)
(fm3-1 :oct 5 :len 4 :gate* 0.75
  c (macro :vol [31 24 16 8]) c (macro none) _ :vol 24 c)
(fm3-2 :oct 6 :len 2
  e (macro :pitch [0 40 80 40]) g (macro :pitch none))
(fm3-3 :oct 6 :len 1 b ~ b)
(fm3-4 :oct 7 :len 1 :vel 10 d _)
(fm3-csm-rate :oct 3 :len 4
  c c _ (glide 4) e g (glide none) c _ c)
